{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DkGoLfW3rYv4wxeEsAX8jA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmation run results at APC 300:\n- MLE Rounds: 164ms (vs before 175ms = -11ms)\n- STARK excl trace: 1297ms (vs before 1331ms = -34ms)\n\nSo we're seeing:\n- Run 1: MLE Rounds 161ms, STARK excl trace 1314ms\n- Run 2: MLE Rounds 164ms, STARK excl trace 1297ms\n\nThe MLE Rounds improvement seems to be real (~11-14ms), but the STARK excl trace improvement fluctuates (17ms in run 1, 34ms in run 2). \n\nThe STARK variation is likely noise from other components like GKR. Looking at the rollback criteria: MLE Rounds is solidly under the 20ms threshold at ~12ms median, while STARK excl trace sits right on the edge at ~26ms median against the 30ms limit. According to the plan, both improvements fall within acceptable bounds, but I need to check what the full instruction says about when to stop iterating.\n\nReviewing the task success criteria, the goal is replacing per-matrix GPU buffer allocation with bulk pre-allocated arena buffers. The plan projected 40-55ms savings at APC 300, but we're only seeing ~13ms—well below expectations. The rollback criteria would trigger at <20ms for MLE Rounds, which we've hit. I should commit and then revert, but first I'm wondering why the actual improvement is so much smaller than the profiling estimate of ~47ms in CUDA memory API overhead. The pool allocator's per-call behavior might be the culprit.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":829,"cache_read_input_tokens":88346,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":829},"output_tokens":30,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a5282c7d-e31f-4078-851d-3bd2d8ef1f99","uuid":"0dbd7097-ef99-497a-9a47-3c1857b81a